---

## Environment (.env) template

Create a `.env` file in the project root. Below is an example template — replace placeholder values with real secrets:

# Server
PORT=8080
API_BASE_URL=http://:8080

# MongoDB
MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/alethea

# JWT
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret_here

# OpenRouter / LLM
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your_openrouter_api_key_here
LLM_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free

# OAuth 
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_client_id
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_google_client_secret
GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:8080/api/auth/google/callback

GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=your_github_client_id
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=your_github_client_secret
GITHUB_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:8080/api/auth/github/callback

# Frontend
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000

---

## Create a .env.local in the client directory for frontend env variables 

# backend url
PUBLIC_NEXT_BACKEND_URL= https://localhost:8080/api

# if news api key is needed
NEXT_PUBLIC_NEWSDATA_API_KEY= your_news_api_key_here